content:
Unlike `request()`/`prepare_request()`, which resolve the active model via `_current_model()` so a `using_model()` selection is honored, `connect()` here always targets `self.wrapped` (the default). In a multi-model registry that diverges: a non-OpenAI default lets a selected `OpenAIResponsesModel` slip past the WebSocket guard (and `getattr(wrapped, 'connect')` raises a bare `AttributeError` rather than the intended message), while an OpenAI default wrongly rejects a custom `connect()` on a selected non-OpenAI model.

Resolving `self._current_model()` first would keep the guard/delegation consistent with how every other method on `TemporalModel` picks the model — though note `_current_model()` can return a raw model-id string, so this branch needs a story for that case too. DBOS/Prefect don't have this problem since they wrap a single model.

@DouweM this is a design call about whether `connect()` should follow `using_model()` selection at all (it's a pre-run setup call), so worth your read before David invests in it.
